From 7b27b0793516e882b6792effcf1a6293b7dd6198 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:11:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/32] Reconstruct xnu-13432 syscall and trap entry points

Add the nine syscalls and one Mach trap that the KDK 27.0.1
kernel.release.vmapple dispatch tables expose beyond the public
xnu-12377.121.6 tree:

  148 pipe2, 149 dup3, 214 fchflagsat, 215 getumask,
  246 aio_readv, 247 aio_writev, 249 fsctlat,
  352 guarded_ftruncate_np, 519 register_uexc_handler,
  Mach trap 108 thread_set_x86_64_compat_trap.

Handler bodies are reconstructed from the reference kernel's
disassembly and DWARF, including the dup_internal/close_fp_for_dup
refactor, ftruncate_internal, fsctlat_internal, and the uexc
registration path.  makesyscalls.sh output matches the reference
sysent table (handler, munge, return type, argument bytes).

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
